WHY THIS LICENCE
----------------

MediaKernel is a translation, not a reimplementation. Its decoders, demuxers and
DSP were written by reading FFmpeg's C source function by function and writing
the equivalent C#, keeping FFmpeg's structures, tables and control flow. A
translation of a work is a derivative of that work, so MediaKernel is bound by
the licence of what it was translated from.

FFmpeg's libavcodec and libavformat are licensed LGPL-2.1-or-later, so that is
MediaKernel's licence too. This is the honest outcome, and it is also the one
the author wants: the people whose work this is built on chose the LGPL, and
MediaKernel does not get to choose differently.

In plain terms: you may use MediaKernel in a closed-source application, as long
as you link it as a library, say that you are using it, and pass on these terms
and any changes you make to MediaKernel itself.


WHOSE WORK THIS IS BUILT ON
---------------------------

FFmpeg - https://ffmpeg.org/
    LGPL-2.1-or-later. The overwhelming majority of this project: libavcodec's
    decoders and DSP, libavformat's demuxers and seeking, libswresample's
    conversion. Individual source files name the C file they were translated
    from.

LAME - https://lame.sourceforge.io/
    LGPL-2.0-or-later. The MP3 encoder under Codecs/MP3/Encoder is a
    translation of LAME, reached through FFmpeg's libmp3lame wrapper.

VideoLAN / VLC - https://www.videolan.org/
    Portions of the LGPL-licensed packetizer and NAL-parsing modules were used
    as a reference alongside the published specifications. Files that cite VLC
    say so in their header comment.

dav1d - https://code.videolan.org/videolan/dav1d
    BSD-2-Clause. Used as a reference for the AV1 decoder.

Xiph.Org Foundation - https://xiph.org/
    BSD-3-Clause. FLAC, Vorbis, Opus and Speex formats and reference behaviour.

The specifications these formats are defined by - ITU-T H.264 and H.265,
ISO/IEC 13818, 14496 and 23008, ETSI TS 102 114, ATSC A/52, RFC 6716 and others
- are the normative source for everything here; the implementations above are
how this project checked its reading of them.


WHAT IS NOT IN THIS REPOSITORY
------------------------------

Some audio and video filters in the author's working tree are translations of
VLC filter modules, and of code VLC in turn took from MPlayer and the LADSPA
SWH plugins. Those upstreams are GPL, not LGPL. They are not published here and
are not in any MediaKernel package, because one GPL-derived file would make the
whole library GPL. None of them is in the demux-decode-present path.

If you want those filters, they need to ship as a separate GPL-licensed
package. That has not been done.


A NOTE ON PROVENANCE
--------------------

Every file that was translated from somebody else's code says so at the top,
and names the file it came from. If you find one that does not, or one whose
attribution is wrong, please open an issue - that is a bug, and a more serious
one than a decoding fault.
